course: dictionary
lesson: 3771
title: The many meanings of follow
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Follow is a verb with several meanings, so the words around it are the best clue. «Each year more than a million wildebeest follow the rain and fresh grass.» Here follow means to go after the rain, moving where it moves.
explain: Follow can also mean to come next in order or time. In «the number that follows 9 is 10», follows means comes next. «The following day» means the next day. To follow rules or instructions is to do what they say, as in «A computer only follows its programs».
explain: Ask which meaning fits, then test it. Put your meaning into the sentence in place of the hard word. If «the number that comes next is 10» still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Follow means to go or come after someone or something.
fact: Follow can mean to come next in order or time, as in «the following week».
fact: To follow rules or instructions is to do exactly what they say.
fact: To follow a story or an explanation is to understand it.
fact: To follow a road or a river is to go along it.
exercise: «The ducklings followed their mother across the pond.» What does followed mean here? | Flew above her | Forgot her | *Went after her | Swam away from her
exercise: «Each year more than a million wildebeest follow the rain and fresh grass.» Find and copy the word that means to go after something. | fresh | grass | million | *follow
exercise: In maths, «the number that follows 9 is 10». What does follows mean? | *Comes next, one more | Comes before | Is the same as | Is much bigger
test: The safety sign says follow the fire drill route. What should you do? | Hide under your desk | Stay where you are and keep reading | *Walk along the marked route to the exit | Go back for your bag
test: «A computer does not feel, want or know anything; it only follows its programs.» What does follows its programs mean? | Feels happy about the programs | Writes brand new programs of its own | Ignores the programs | *Does exactly what the programs tell it
exam: «It was hard to follow the explanation, so Mia read it again.» What does follow mean here? | To copy it onto paper | To throw it away | *To understand it | To walk behind the explanation
